GitHub issue body:
## Summary
Create an intelligence accessibility map covering llm-wikis, resource intelligence, and document intelligence so the weekly review in #2089 can verify not just freshness, but actual discoverability and usability.

## Why
Knowledge only helps if agents and humans can find it quickly from the machine/repo context where work is happening. Important intelligence is currently at risk of being fragmented across repos, docs, indexes, transcripts, or machine-local paths.

## Scope
- inventory the primary intelligence assets and their canonical locations
- define the entry points agents/humans should use to find them
- identify broken links, path drift, stale indexes, or missing sync points
- define accessibility checks for the weekly review
- identify intelligence that is trapped in non-canonical or hard-to-discover locations
- recommend improvements to retrieval/discoverability

## Deliverables
- intelligence accessibility map
- weekly accessibility checklist
- list of retrieval/discoverability gaps
- recommendations for canonical access paths

## Parent
- Parent issue: #2089


